{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations","id":899991,"title":"Transmutations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-26T06:52:00-07:00","id":899991,"title":"Transmutations","content":"Preview here: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/prometheantransmutations/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/prometheantransmutations/</a><br /> <br /> So what do you guys think? I feel like it'll be really interesting, especially for Transmutations like Vitality where everything seemed to be upgrades of the first 2-3 powers, or Alchemicus where many powers weren't really interesting as a single power.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So let's try and see what Alembics could go in each Transmutation from the first ed. Corebook<br /> <br /> <b>Alchemicus:</b><br /> -Perfecting (Master's Tool, Fortification, ???)<br /> -Changing (Transformation, ???, Resize)<br /> -Destroying (Dissolve, Degradation, Flesh to Stone)<br /> -Rebuilding (Identification, Alteration, Spark of Life)<br /> <br /> <b>Corporeum:</b><br /> -Dexterity (Swift feet, uncanny dex, Rarified Grace)<br /> -Holistic Body (Autonomic Control, ??? Human Flesh)<br /> -Regeneration (Regeneration, Rejuvenation, ???)<br /> -Reflexes (Ingrained Reflexes, Perfected Reflexes, Serpent's Strike)<br /> <br /> <b>Deception:</b><br /> -Chameleon (Chameleon Skin, Move Silently, Vitreous Humor)<br /> -Doppleganger (Color of Man, Mimic's Voice, Mask)<br /> -Ghost (Incognito, Leave no Trace, False Tracks)<br /> -?????<br /> <br /> <b>Disquietism:</b><br /> -Quell (Alembic, Soothe Disquiet, Quell Disquiet)<br /> -Give (Rabid Rage, Iago's Whisper, Nameless Dread)<br /> -Scapegoat (Scapegoat, Progenitor's Curse, ???)<br /> -Release (Tension in the Air, Mass Hysteria, Shape Disquiet)<br /> <br /> <b>Electrification:</b><br /> -Lightning Bolts ('nouf said)<br /> -Gathering energy (Insulator, Power Sink, Blackout)<br /> -Releasing Energy (Jolt, Generator, Regulator)<br /> -????<br /> <br /> <b>Mesmerism:</b><br /> Well.... hard to tell since Prommies no longer have direct mind control....hmm...<br /> <br /> <b>Metamorphosis:</b> (I'd be surprised to be wrong on this one)<br /> -Adapt<br /> -Change into an animal<br /> -Create Armor<br /> -Change Appearance<br /> <br /> <b>Sensorium:</b><br /> -Sight<br /> -Touch<br /> -Smell &amp; Taste<br /> -Hearing<br /> <br /> <b>Vitality:</b><br /> -Destroying stuff (Fist of talos, Titan's Throw, Battering Ram)<br /> -Jumping far (there's a mention in Mortal Remains that a Promethean jumped <i>reaaaaaaaally </i>far)<br /> -Punching hard (Vigor, Bludgeon, Defenestration Blow)<br /> -Too strong for the League (Thunderclap Blow, Wrath of Hecatonshire)<br /> <br /> <b>Vulcanus:</b><br /> -Sensing (All the Sense [Thing], Sigil on the Wind and Firebrand?)<br /> -Manipulate Flames (Animate Firetouched, Firegrasp, Trigger Firestorm!)<br /> -Manipulate Pyros (Share Pyros, The Greater Need, Pyros Imp)<br /> -Refine Pyros (Electroshock Recharge, Crucible of the Will and Sublimate Phlogiston)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T07:03:11-07:00","id":899995,"title":"","content":"I want all of my characters to Calcify the &quot;Jumping Far&quot; ability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T07:19:27-07:00","id":900008,"title":"","content":"I wonder if Calcifying an Alembic has any effect on the Promethean's Redeemed self. Maybe something like allowing you to access the Persistent effect for a scene with a willpower point? Or is that too &quot;missing the point&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T09:53:34-07:00","id":900143,"title":"","content":"That would certainly be an interesting way to pull something of your past life over into the new reality of your human life. But that's past endgame so doubt it really needs to be explored.<br /> <br /> I really dig how Transmutations appear to work, with choosing an Alembic and getting a persistent effect and charging it with Pyros to change yourself or the world around you. God, I need this book like whoa.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T11:30:10-07:00","id":900203,"title":"","content":"I really like the structure. I do sort of wish that the Distillations either followed a clear progression, with each &quot;higher&quot; distillation being an enhanced form of those previous, or alternatively that the Pyros costs weren't locked in at 0 &gt; 1 &gt; 2 &gt; 3. As it stands it feels like it's supposed to be more Pyros = more potent effect, but instead it's more Pyros = different effect, with no clear correlation between which effects are cheaper and which are more expensive. Why does superior climbing cost more Pyros than water breathing? If it's just because one of them had to cost more for it to fit the structure, then maybe the structure is too rigid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-26-2016, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T11:47:51-07:00","id":900228,"title":"","content":"Looks cool, though I'm concerned about scaling. As written there doesn't seem to be much room for new Alembics or Distillations within a Transmutation. Like, how would a custom Distillation work? Would it replace an existing one, be added, get the middle finger and be refused outright?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations?p=900203#post900203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really like the structure. I do sort of wish that the Distillations either followed a clear progression, with each &quot;higher&quot; distillation being an enhanced form of those previous, or alternatively that the Pyros costs weren't locked in at 0 &gt; 1 &gt; 2 &gt; 3. As it stands it feels like it's supposed to be more Pyros = more potent effect, but instead it's more Pyros = different effect, with no clear correlation between which effects are cheaper and which are more expensive. Why does superior climbing cost more Pyros than water breathing? If it's just because one of them had to cost more for it to fit the structure, then maybe the structure is too rigid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking at it again, yeah. At least on the surface it appears the costs are kinda arbitrary. I mean, I won't challenge Procrustian Shape being the top, but what is the narrative justification for wall climbing being 'above' water breathing? Is it the bigger physical adjustment, is that was decides it? <br /> <br /> Bringing it around to my original question. What if I wanted to burrow? That seems within this Alembics purview, but how would I decide where to put it? or how to price it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 05-26-2016, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T12:20:37-07:00","id":900247,"title":"","content":"Well, maybe there's a type of power we haven't seen yet? Something akin to Devotions or Rites or Attainments. Powers which are easier to homebrew than Alembics. No one complained that the Disciplines in Blood &amp; Smoke were too strict after all.<br /> <br /> So maybe? Who knows","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T12:33:51-07:00","id":900259,"title":"","content":"Also, I <i>think </i>\u200bthat it's more like a battery that you're filling up. Maybe <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13\" data-vbnamecard=\"13\">blackhatmatt</a> could answer that? If I want to activate Procrustean Shape, I pay 3 pyros, does that activate both previous powers too? Or is that only for PS?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blog Post</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ul><li>Everything requires Pyros expenditure, and all Transmutations get more impressive <b>as you pump</b> more Pyros into them.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blog Post</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Oh, sorry, that system isn\u2019t specified here: For the most part, once you <b>charge</b> a Distillation it\u2019s on for a scene.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T12:36:27-07:00","id":900261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations?p=900247#post900247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, maybe there's a type of power we haven't seen yet? Something akin to Devotions or Rites or Attainments. Powers which are easier to homebrew than Alembics. No one complained that the Disciplines in Blood &amp; Smoke were too strict after all.<br /> <br /> So maybe? Who knows</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, certainly, I'm just speculating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T13:20:15-07:00","id":900296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations?p=900259#post900259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I <i>think </i>\u200bthat it's more like a battery that you're filling up. Maybe <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13\" data-vbnamecard=\"13\">blackhatmatt</a> could answer that? If I want to activate Procrustean Shape, I pay 3 pyros, does that activate both previous powers too? Or is that only for PS?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You got it. Spend 3 Pyros and you charge the whole Alembic, not just the one Distillation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T13:33:01-07:00","id":900307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations?p=900296#post900296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You got it. Spend 3 Pyros and you charge the whole Alembic, not just the one Distillation.</div> </div> </div> </div>What made you decide not price them each at 1 Pyros, then let the player decide the order in which they activate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T14:33:41-07:00","id":900365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations?p=900296#post900296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You got it. Spend 3 Pyros and you charge the whole Alembic, not just the one Distillation.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems troublesome for Aparte because it effectively costs 3 Pyros if you want to climb walls but still breathe air (1 to switch on Scuttling Spider and Blessing of Tethys and 1 to reverse the effect of Blessing of Tethys) but only 2 if you want to climb walls and breathe water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T14:45:15-07:00","id":900376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations?p=900365#post900365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems troublesome for Aparte because it effectively costs 3 Pyros if you want to climb walls but still breathe air (1 to switch on Scuttling Spider and Blessing of Tethys and 1 to reverse the effect of Blessing of Tethys) but only 2 if you want to climb walls and breathe water.</div> </div> </div> </div>It also costs 4 Pyros to activate Procrustean Shape without suffocating. I'm 100% certain that's not intended design.<br /> <br /> Edit: Other note, the Passive function says &quot;The Pariah cannot breathe water or survive in a vacuum without charging the Alembic&quot;, but even with the Alembic charged it's not possible to survive in a vacuum.<br /> <br /> Double Edit: Some other questions/comments:<ul><li>Since I assume you cannot turn off Distillations at will (otherwise returning to breathing air wouldn't cost Pyros) that makes it possible to do something like activate Procrustean Shape to reach something, roll one success then be stuck with a four foot arm and -1 in combat (though I've no idea why longer reach on one arm makes you worse at combat). How would I counteract that? Would have have to pay 3 Pyros again to turn it off or switch the version?</li> <li>Malleable Skeleton mentions use in conjunction with other alterations, is that just a note in case of Exceptional Success? Or is it possible to reactivate? And if so, at what cost?</li> <li>I have to wonder about the balance between alterations. Long Arms grants +1 Defense, which is pretty negligible, especially for 3 Pyros. Altered Body gives successes in Armor, which is fucking tremendous. For instance, if I rolled three successes my options would be: +1 Defense, 10 Foot Arm, +3 Speed, Squeeze through gaps, or <b>+3/+3 Armor.</b> Of these things two are underwhelming, two highly conditional, and one is fucking amazing!</li> </ul>The more I think about this the more punishing the structure seems. Unless Pyros is fucking everywhere 3 is a lot to pay to reach one object that is far away, or gain a tiny boost in speed. If it were +[Successes] Defense, or a speed multiplier that'd be another thing, but as is it reads like a power that'll disappoint often.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 05-26-2016, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T14:47:31-07:00","id":900378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations?p=900376#post900376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also costs 4 Pyros to activate Procrustean Shape without suffocating. I'm 100% certain that's not intended design.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence my confusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T15:38:44-07:00","id":900416,"title":"","content":"The perfect Alembic for deep sea probes who become Unfleshed and forgot how to swim as the price. Man, how many times has that old trope been played?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T15:41:12-07:00","id":900418,"title":"","content":"Overall, I'm glad to see a new structure to the system. I'm hoping that this isn't what's sitting in layout, given all the flaws mentioned here, but overall it's a turn toward a more exciting and thematic power set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T16:57:16-07:00","id":900470,"title":"","content":"Even if it is what's sitting in layout, it's an easy fix. Just allow postponed activation if you activate an upper level without passing by the lower one (so instead of pumping 1&gt;1&gt;1 you pump 2 or 3 one shot).<br /> <br /> It's a quick and easy fix without real problems. I'd allow it as an ST","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-26T21:33:31-07:00","id":900665,"title":"","content":"Missing Alembics:<br /> Electrification could have a magnetism one, or maybe a &quot;form-of&quot; that could allow travel through the power grid.<br /> Mesmerism is pretty hard. Maybe an entrancement Alembic that leaves the subject dazed, fixated, and insensate. Perhaps an Aggressive Meme-like vector for ideas and inspiration, that Inspires subjects who get infected.<br /> Spiritus seems cut and dry, either Alembics by target splat, or by wards and disguises and THIRD THING. <br /> Are Aes, Cobalus, et al., getting their old Transmissions ported over?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T04:02:08-07:00","id":900819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations?p=900365#post900365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems troublesome for Aparte because it effectively costs 3 Pyros if you want to climb walls but still breathe air (1 to switch on Scuttling Spider and Blessing of Tethys and 1 to reverse the effect of Blessing of Tethys) but only 2 if you want to climb walls and breathe water.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I see your confusion, I guess, but the intent isn't that you have to use the lower-Pyros Distillations to charge the higher-level ones. If you just want to climb walls, spend the 2 Pyros and charge Scuttling Spider, but leave your lungs alone. Same would be true of other Distillations; you don't need to use the 1 to use the 2, but you can if you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T07:38:23-07:00","id":900950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations?p=900819#post900819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see your confusion, I guess, but the intent isn't that you have to use the lower-Pyros Distillations to charge the higher-level ones. If you just want to climb walls, spend the 2 Pyros and charge Scuttling Spider, but leave your lungs alone. Same would be true of other Distillations; you don't need to use the 1 to use the 2, but you can if you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, what Matt said.<br /> <br /> I believe it's a reflexive action limited by your Pyros-per-turn to charge the Alembic, but an instant action to <i>use</i> the Distillation; you don't <i>need </i>to activate it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-27T08:01:34-07:00","id":900970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations?p=900950#post900950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, what Matt said.<br /> <br /> I believe it's a reflexive action limited by your Pyros-per-turn to charge the Alembic, but an instant action to <i>use</i> the Distillation; you don't <i>need </i>to activate it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, ok. That makes more sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T01:59:47-07:00","id":901887,"title":"","content":"On first reading yesterday - <b>Do I get it right that you <i>cannot</i> have your Transmutation left with you after you change Refinements? </b>Even if you studied Aurum for months, you need to forget all you discovered with Mesmersim, just because you change Refinement?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T02:04:36-07:00","id":901888,"title":"","content":"No. If you want to keep them after changing Refinements, you Calcify them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T02:08:54-07:00","id":901889,"title":"","content":"Re-read the bit about calcifying the Alembics Wyrd. When you change refinements you change your base Transmutations, but while following one, you can make some of it permanent to your character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T02:14:59-07:00","id":901893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations?p=901888#post901888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. If you want to keep them after changing Refinements, you Calcify them.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gullinbursti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations?p=901889#post901889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re-read the bit about calcifying the Alembics Wyrd. When you change refinements you change your base Transmutations, but while following one, you can make some of it permanent to your character.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Question is how high is price of Calcifying - your vampire or werewolf do not need to &quot;lock&quot; they powers to not lose them...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T02:21:11-07:00","id":901898,"title":"","content":"Probably less than learning all but the most basic of transmutations in the original Promethean. Remember joining a Refinement didn't automatically give you transmutations in 1E, you had to buy them to keep them. If you studied gold for several months and then moved to iron, without experience expenditure, you didn't gain transmutations from gold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T03:36:04-07:00","id":901926,"title":"","content":"Also, even if you don't keep the Alembics, you still retain the &quot;slots&quot; you earned. If you master three Roles, you have access to every Alembic available in that Refinement's Transmutations, and if you change Refinements, you don't lose that progress. Which makes receding to Stannum hella tempting when things go pear-shaped.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T08:18:35-07:00","id":902057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations?p=901893#post901893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question is how high is price of Calcifying - your vampire or werewolf do not need to &quot;lock&quot; they powers to not lose them...</div> </div> </div> </div>Calcifying them would be the equivalent of buying them in 1st Ed. Under this system you don't actually spend experience to learn Transmutations, you gain them automatically simply by being in a Refinement and fulfilling the Roles therein. The price of Calcifying, however high or low, appears to be the 'only' price associated with Transmutations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T08:46:10-07:00","id":902072,"title":"","content":"WHAT? I get Transmutations for free?! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T08:50:35-07:00","id":902077,"title":"","content":"Yep. Effectively a \u201ctry before you buy\u201d setup. <br /> <br /> One minor irritant: you go through the trouble to master several Roles, making more Alembics available to you; then you switch Refinements and are back at one Alembic. I really hope it's easier to master a Role than it is to Calcify an Alembic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-28-2016, 11:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T11:00:12-07:00","id":902141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> blackhatmatt</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> When you master three Roles (be they from the Refinement you\u2019re on, or one from three different Refinement), you get access to both of the full Transmutations associated with any Refinement you switch to. So let\u2019s so you\u2019re on Plumbum, master it (all three Roles, go you). You\u2019ve got access to all four Alembics in both Disquietism and Electrification.<br /> Then you decide you want to get freaky with it, so you switch to Argentum. Now you\u2019ve got access to all four Alembics in Spiritus and Sensorium. It doesn\u2019t matter what Refinement you go to; once you\u2019ve mastered three Roles, you have access to all the powers in that Refinement.<br /> But that alone won\u2019t make you human. <img src=\"https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/72x72/1f642.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, you're still at four Alembics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-28T17:14:06-07:00","id":902378,"title":"","content":"A mixed question. About Roles - I seem to have confusion over them. Now, there seem to be three roles per Refinement. If you take all three Roles, you can learn all eight affinity Transmutations. But, after a while, Roles grow stale. Now, about this point is where I'm confused - can you keep this stale Role when you swap Refinements? I thought that was so when I read Roles the first time, but now it doesn't make sense to get extra power from the wrong Refinement's Roles. <br /> <br /> Can you Calcify one ability without switching your Refinement? Can you Cacify an ability without actually taking it?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T06:29:44-07:00","id":902667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations?p=902378#post902378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mixed question. About Roles - I seem to have confusion over them. Now, there seem to be three roles per Refinement. If you take all three Roles, you can learn all eight affinity Transmutations. But, after a while, Roles grow stale. Now, about this point is where I'm confused - can you keep this stale Role when you swap Refinements? I thought that was so when I read Roles the first time, but now it doesn't make sense to get extra power from the wrong Refinement's Roles.<br /> <br /> Can you Calcify one ability without switching your Refinement? Can you Cacify an ability without actually taking it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> OK, lemme try to unpack this a little, using an example.<br /> <br /> Avalon (one of the characters in my PtC game, and also the POV character in the short story &quot;Dedication&quot; in the <b>Firestorm Anthology</b>) is on Aurum. There are three Roles - Follower, Companion, and Leader. When she starts the Refinement, she's studying the Companion Role (it's the closest to what she was created <i>for</i>, so it's what she knows, which means it's a logical place to start). The two Transmutations in Aurum are Deception and Mesmerism. Since, as a starting character, she's got no Roles under her belt, she gets to pick one Alembic from each Transmutation. She picks Assimilation from Deception and Eros from Mesmerism.<br /> <br /> The chronicle progresses, and she gets close to mastering Companion, but then flubs something critical (in game terms, she misses the milestone that would let her master the Role). She decides she really doesn't <i>get</i> people very well, and she needs to understand her own magical nature. She switches to Mercurius (note that since this is a complex Refinement, she'd need a tutor or something, but one of her throngmates is on the Refinement and can teach her). Since she hasn't mastered any Roles yet, she gets the same deal: One Alembic each from both Transmutations of Mercurius (Alchemicus and Vulcanus, as it happens; she picks Stone and Ignus Aspiritus, respectively). She's trying for the Craftsman Role. She achieves it, which means she gets a new Alembic in each Transmutation (let's say she picks Elixir from Alchemicus and Cauterio from Vulcanus).<br /> <br /> Now, she's got a choice, here. She can stay on Mercurius and try for a different Role (there's some benefit to completely mastering a Refinement). She can stay on Mercurius and <i>not</i> try for a different Role; she's mastered Craftsman which means that as long as she stays in that Role, her Disquiet is much lessened...but she also runs the risk of being stuck in a rut, which can have consequences later (for the record, this doesn't happen the second you master a Role; my personal feeling is that if you master a Role you shouldn't get stuck in a rut unless and until it makes narrative sense, but more on that another time). She can also switch Refinements.<br /> <br /> Let's say that she feels she's got a good enough grip on people, by way of whatever she learned on Mercurius, that she wants another go at Aurum. It's a basic Refinement, so she doesn't need a teacher or anything, just a little time to switch gears (tee-hee. That's funny because she's clockwork). She goes back to Aurum, again shooting for the Companion Role, and she picks Assimilation and Eros again (she doesn't <i>have</i> to, but the player figures that they feel familiar). <br /> <br /> Eventually she masters Companion, meaning she gets <i>another</i> Alembic slot within Aurum. So let's say she picks Doppelganger and Penthos (Deception and Mesmerism, respectively), for while she's finishing up on Aurum. Same choice as before: Stay on Aurum and switch Roles, stay on Aurum and risk becoming stuck, or switch Refinements.<br /> <br /> Avalon decides that, while she does want to master Aurum eventually, she'll be better able to do that with a firm understanding of why people fuck things up so badly. That induces her to adopt Cobalus. The Transmutations there are Contamination and, hey, look at that, Mesmerism. But, because she hasn't been on Cobalus and mastered any Roles there, she only gets one Alembic from each Transmutation (she can choose to keep a Mesmerism one that she's already used or pick a new one, either's fine).<br /> <br /> However, since Cobalus doesn't use Deception, Avalon will lose her Assimilation, Anonymity, and Doppelganger Alembics. She's grown quite fond of Assimilation, so she decides to spend some Vitriol Experiences to calcify it. Now, the Assimilation Alembic is permanently part of her makeup. When she switches to whatever Refinement, that Alembic does not count against her total. That means that, if you're keeping track, she's now on Cobalus. She gets one Alembic from Contamination, one from Mesmerism, and she's got Assimilation permanently.<br /> <br /> If she switches back to Aurum, though, Assimilation doesn't count against her total. As such, since she's mastered one Role there, she'd get two Alembics from each Transmutation, <i>plus</i> Assimilation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","user":"blackhatmatt","date":".  Ha-ha. Was actually explicating from an older version of the rules. Is correct now. Moar coffee. 05-29-2016, 09:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T06:40:59-07:00","id":902672,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the responce, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13\" data-vbnamecard=\"13\">blackhatmatt</a>. That makes much more sense to me! Just one more question - could Avalon have Calcified Assimilation before switching to Cobalus, and thus gained access to the fourth Deceptionism Alembic? Or is that just something you can do when swapping Refinements? Related, can you &quot;swap&quot; to your current Refinement and switch what Alembics you know if you don't want to leave, but want a different take on the matter?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T06:53:35-07:00","id":902684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations?p=902672#post902672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for the responce, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar13_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13\" data-vbnamecard=\"13\">blackhatmatt</a>. That makes much more sense to me! Just one more question - could Avalon have Calcified Assimilation before switching to Cobalus, and thus gained access to the fourth Deceptionism Alembic? Or is that just something you can do when swapping Refinements? Related, can you &quot;swap&quot; to your current Refinement and switch what Alembics you know if you don't want to leave, but want a different take on the matter?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, sure. You can calcify any time you have the XP to do it, which then opens up another slot in the Transmutation for you. <br /> <br /> The second question...hmm. I actually don't think we address that. I would allow a player to do that, sure, though it'd probably require a scene and some cool roleplaying just to explain the character's though process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T06:59:22-07:00","id":902690,"title":"","content":"Cool! Thanks again for the answers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T08:04:12-07:00","id":902720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations?p=902672#post902672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Related, can you &quot;swap&quot; to your current Refinement and switch what Alembics you know if you don't want to leave, but want a different take on the matter?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would make sense to me if you changed Roles within the Refinement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T08:21:10-07:00","id":902733,"title":"","content":"I imagined that they actually couldn't switch Alembics within a Refinement when I did preliminary design, but this was contingent on the Promethean reverting to Stannum and then re-adopting her Refinement. <br /> <br /> I'll also note that Disquietism and Electrification are two of the most utilitarian and survival-focused Promethean Transmutations, and have their entire suite of effects available <i>de facto</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T09:05:03-07:00","id":902751,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't Iron be the most survival focused? Or Copper? *blink*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T11:04:46-07:00","id":902817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations?p=902751#post902751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't Iron be the most survival focused? Or Copper? *blink*</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, sure, you've got a point, but there are lots of things you need to survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T11:56:40-07:00","id":902926,"title":"","content":"I didn't mean... um... well, the entire game is about survival in some manner or another. I'm just not really sure how Disquietism and Electrification are considered survival oriented. That seems like a leap from what I understand of those two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-29T13:11:41-07:00","id":902963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations?p=902926#post902926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't mean... um... well, the entire game is about survival in some manner or another. I'm just not really sure how Disquietism and Electrification are considered survival oriented. That seems like a leap from what I understand of those two.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, from a human perspective of survival, but consider that some of the biggest threats to Prometheans come down to &quot;Disquiet&quot; and &quot;stuff that can be hit with a bolt of lightning&quot; and you'll see where I'm coming from. There are few problems an EMP won't solve, though it might not be the best solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T00:03:38-07:00","id":903308,"title":"","content":"So it's sounding like we've got the same Transmutations; it's just that they're structured differently? That is, each Refinement is linked to two Transmutations, and those two Transmutations have the same names and overall concepts as the ones that were associated with them back in 1e. But instead of an assortment of dot-rated powers, you've got the \u201cfour Alembics with four Distillations each\u201d structure. <br /> <br /> 1) Do Prometheans still have Bestowments (that is, powers tied to their Lineages/Humours rather than their Refinements)? If so, are they structured like Transmutations? Obviously, they wouldn't have \u201cswap which Bestowments you have when you change Lineages\u201d, as I doubt that 2e Prometheans can swap Lineages any more than 1e Prometheans could; but they might still have some sort of Alembic/Distillation setup. <br /> <br /> 2) Do Centimani get Transmutations? If not, what <i> do</i> they get? <br /> <br /> 3) The <b>Demon Storyteller's Guide</b> mentions that alchemists have access to Transmutations. How does that work, since they probably don't have Refinements? <br /> <br /> 4) The <b>Demon Storytellers Guide</b> also mentions that alchemists can make potions and the like. Can Prometheans do that too? <br /> <br /> 5) I'm guessing that \u201cPandoran Transmutations\u201d are being replaced by Dread Powers?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 05-31-2016, 01:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T01:21:51-07:00","id":903329,"title":"","content":"I recall something somewhere in these pages that Centimanus was no longer a Refinement, and that they couldn't learn the powers of the Pandorans, because those were no longer Transmutations. If that is the case, perhaps a centimanus stays on his Refinement. <br /> <br /> Now, what I'd do with<i> that </i>is allow the Freak to charge Alembics with Flux. He would risk Pilgrimage points, but he'd save on Pyros, and access special Distillations. Aptare opens up all the old Hundred Hands choices. Maybe Eros drives victims to debase themselves, or Corporeum causes monstrous deformations of shape and size.<br /> <br /> What actually got done, I dunno.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T08:48:33-07:00","id":903574,"title":"","content":"I was wondering about Centimani as well. It doesn't seem like they'd be interested in Roles - quite the reverse - so they'd likely be weaker in these Transmutations than regular Prometheans. Is there another way to get access to them? Can Centimani get another sort of power (and if so can regular Prometheans use it, with a hit to their Pilgrimmage?). Or are Centimani simply weaker?<br /> <br /> <br /> I like this system because it ties your powers to your Pilgrimmage; your alchemy parallels your learning to become human. Even those who might disdain the end point have a reason to undertake the journey (ironically, almost certainly the <i>same</i> reason for their disdain).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":". 05-30-2016, 11:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T09:55:30-07:00","id":903616,"title":"","content":"Always number your questions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations?p=903308#post903308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) Do Prometheans still have Bestowments (that is, powers tied to their Lineages/Humours rather than their Refinements)? If so, are they structured like Transmutations? Obviously, they wouldn't have \u201cswap which Bestowments you have when you change Lineages\u201d, as I doubt that 2e Prometheans can swap Lineages any more than 1e Prometheans could; but they might still have some sort of Alembic/Distillation setup.<br /> <br /> 2) Do Centimani get Transmutations? If not, what <i> do</i> they get?<br /> <br /> 3) The <b>Demon Storyteller's Guide</b> mentions that alchemists have access to Transmutations. How does that work, since they probably don't have Refinements?<br /> <br /> 4) The <b>Demon Storytellers Guide</b> also mentions that alchemists can make potions and the like. Can Prometheans do that too?<br /> <br /> 5)I'm guessing that \u201cPandoran Transmutations\u201d are being replaced by Dread Powers?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Yes. No. <br /> <br /> 2) Yes, but they have one Transmutation (Flux) and that has more far-reaching effects. <br /> <br /> 3) They have access to individual Distillations, rather than whole Alembics. <br /> <br /> 4) Theoretically, a Promethean could make an alchemical preparation, but they usually have better things to do with their Vitriol. <br /> <br /> 5) Yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T14:29:41-07:00","id":903779,"title":"","content":"1)are there such thing as transmutations not tied to refinements, like if a promethean during his pilgrimage finds a way to manipulate the world differently,does he has to tie the new transmutations he made to his refinement","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-30T22:28:20-07:00","id":903964,"title":"","content":"Some followup: <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations?p=903616#post903616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Yes. No. <br /> <br /> 2) Yes, but they have one Transmutation (Flux) and that has more far-reaching effects. <br /> <br /> 3) They have access to individual Distillations, rather than whole Alembics. <br /> <br /> 4) Theoretically, a Promethean could make an alchemical preparation, but they usually have better things to do with their Vitriol. <br /> <br /> 5) Yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u24f5 So, are Bestowments still handled as they were in 1e? <br /> <br /> \u24f7 So an alchemist would buy Distillations of an Alembic the way vampires buy dots in Disciplines?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T06:28:25-07:00","id":904118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations?p=903964#post903964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> \u24f5 So, are Bestowments still handled as they were in 1e?<br /> <br /> \u24f7 So an alchemist would buy Distillations of an Alembic the way vampires buy dots in Disciplines?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Inasmuch as they're singular powers defined by Lineage, yes. A lot of the systems have changed, and every Lineage has a choice of two Bestowments.<br /> <br /> 2) Not exactly, they'd &quot;buy&quot; them as discrete powers. Remember that alchemists aren't designed to be playable so they don't spend XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T07:31:47-07:00","id":904138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations?p=904118#post904118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Not exactly, they'd &quot;buy&quot; them as discrete powers. Remember that alchemists aren't designed to be playable so they don't spend XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>2) But if they <i>were</i>, about how would they do so? 3XP per &quot;level&quot; and/or Needing to spend a point of &quot;acquired&quot; Vitriol?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T14:18:05-07:00","id":904442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations?p=904118#post904118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Inasmuch as they're singular powers defined by Lineage, yes. A lot of the systems have changed, and every Lineage has a choice of two Bestowments.</div> </div> </div> </div>One last question: in 1e, a Promethean could acquire more Bestowments later on; and if s/he takes a Bestowment of another Lineage, that Lineage's Humour is strengthened (with the strengthening handled entirely through roleplaying: take a Frankenstein Bestowment and you have more of a temper). Does 2e still do this?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations?p=904118#post904118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Not exactly, they'd \u201cbuy\u201d them as discrete powers. Remember that alchemists aren't designed to be playable so they don't spend XP.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations?p=904138#post904138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) But if they <i>were</i>, about how would they do so? 3XP per \u201clevel\u201d and/or Needing to spend a point of \u201cacquired\u201d Vitriol?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that Vitriol is an in-game quantity that can be stolen (unless you've changed that in 2e?) and that how it's earned tends to drive characters' behavior, I'm curious about this, too. My <i>guess</i> is that a playable alchemist would \u201cbuy\u201d Distillations with Vitriol (not Experience), similar to how Prometheans Calcify Alembics using Vitriol.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T20:37:11-07:00","id":904685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations?p=904442#post904442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One last question: in 1e, a Promethean could acquire more Bestowments later on; and if s/he takes a Bestowment of another Lineage, that Lineage's Humour is strengthened (with the strengthening handled entirely through roleplaying: take a Frankenstein Bestowment and you have more of a temper). Does 2e still do this?</div> </div> </div> </div>If I recall correctly from the last time this question was asked, the answer is no, because Bestowments can no longer be purchased.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T18:07:02-07:00","id":905293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations?p=904118#post904118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1) Inasmuch as they're singular powers defined by Lineage, yes. A lot of the systems have changed, and every Lineage has a choice of two Bestowments.<br /> <br /> 2) Not exactly, they'd &quot;buy&quot; them as discrete powers. Remember that alchemists aren't designed to be playable so they don't spend XP.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/899991-transmutations?p=904138#post904138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2) But if they <i>were</i>, about how would they do so? 3XP per &quot;level&quot; and/or Needing to spend a point of &quot;acquired&quot; Vitriol?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. I imagine a lot of people will want to play alchemists once in a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}